# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Phase 9 is complete. There is no current implementation phase until a new phase document is added under `docs/`.

Do feature work on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Do not start a previously listed Phase 10 or later. New phases are defined as we go.

Until a later phase explicitly changes them, keep these constraints: Stripe **test mode** only (no live keys), no seller bank payouts, no refund/chargeback workflows, no authority integrations. Never trust the browser for payment status, bid time, or quota availability. Never delete quota ledger rows.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current request.

Stop at the end of each phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
